We guarantee a high level of availability (99.9%) and ensure that our solution integrates with existing systems of information, including civil status, town planning, EDM, and user directories. Our team employs PRINCE2 and Agile Scrum methodologies, has certification in PMP ITIL V4, and is compliant with all relevant regulations, including GDPR and the EU AI Act.

Our pricing model uses standard daily rates, targeting a gross margin percentage of 28%, and we assume maintaining the target gross margin percentage. We have experience with public procurement in several EU jurisdictions, including Italy, France, Germany, Belgium, and EU institutions, and comply with the AI Act of the European Union.

In conclusion, our proposal meets all the requirements and constraints specified by the City of Belval, providing an innovative and sustainable artificial intelligence solution that improves the efficiency and quality of administrative services while ensuring data protection and sovereignty. We are confident that our team can deliver a high-quality solution within the specified budget and timeline, contributing to the City of Belval's goals of reducing its environmental footprint and upholding social responsibility and AI ethics.
